          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong exponentiable topos
            is a generalization of the notion of an exponentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            and can be viewed as a (topological) “space”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that behaves well with respect to the construction of mapping spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is called
              %em exponentiable
              (in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of Grothendieck toposes
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GrTop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GrTop
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{-}\times\mathcal{E}
              has a right 2-adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (_{-})^\mathcal{E}
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                More concretely,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is exponentiable if there exists a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (_{-})^\mathcal{E}
                such that for all toposes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒢
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F},\mathcal{G}
                the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathcal{F}\times\mathcal{E},\mathcal{G})
                is (naturally) equivalent as a category to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℱ
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒢
                          %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathcal{F},\mathcal{G}^\mathcal{E})
            %li
              %p
                By setting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}=\mathcal{S}
                , the base topos, one sees from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{G}^\mathcal{E})=Hom(\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{E},\mathcal{G})=Hom(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{G})
                that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒢
                        %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}^\mathcal{E}
                is indeed a “mapping space” whose
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} points
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphisms
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒢
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{G}
            %li
              %p
                The concept generalizes to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
                (cf.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#A15"} Anel 2015
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#AJ18"} Anel-Lejay 2018
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Lurie18"} Lurie 2018
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Interestingly, in the category of locales exponentiability of a locale
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            hinges on the existence of the single exponential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^X
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpinski space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            exists for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^X
            exists.
          %p
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GrTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GrTop
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos+for+the+theory+of+objects"} object classifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]
            takes over the role of the Sierpinski space and we have the following
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is exponentiable iff the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E}
              exists.
          %p
            This result is due to Johnstone-Joyal (
            %a{:href => "#JJ82"}> 1982
            , p.282) and occurs as theorem 4.3.1 of Johnstone (
            %a{:href => "#J02"}> 2002, vol.1 p.433
            ).
          %p
            The following theorem pursues this analogy and generalizes a result of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"} Martin Hyland
            on locales (
            %a{:href => "#Hyland81"}> 1981
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is an exponentiable object in the 2-category of Grothendieck toposes and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+category"} continuous category
          %p
            This result is due to Johnstone-Joyal (
            %a{:href => "#JJ82"}> 1982
            ) and occurs as theorem 4.4.5 of Johnstone (
            %a{:href => "#J02"}> 2002, p.748
            ).
          %p Exponentiability is a local property:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %ol
              %li
                If a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is exponentiable so is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
                for any object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{E}
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}/X
                is exponentiable and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to 1
                is an epimorphism, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is exponentiable as well.
          %p
            This occurs as lemma 4.2 in Johnstone-Joyal (
            %a{:href => "#JJ82"}> 1982
            , p.281).
          %p Continuity also leaves a lattice-theoretic trace:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is exponentiable then the lattice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobjects
              of any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in\mathcal{E}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+lattice"} continuous
          %p
            This occurs as lemma 5.1 in Johnstone-Joyal (
            %a{:href => "#JJ82"}> 1982
            , p.287).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Since
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+categories"} locally finitely presentable categories
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+category"} continuous
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+topos"} coherent toposes
                are locally finitely presentable (cf. Johnstone (
                %a{:href => "#J02"}> 2002, p.915
                )) it follows that
                = succeed "." do
                  %em coherent toposes are exponentiable
            %li
              %p
                By the same reasoning all functor categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}}
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                are exponentiable since they are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+toposes"} presheaf toposes
                on small categories.
            %li
              %p
                An example of the latter is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+topos"} Sierpinski topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒮
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}^2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℱ
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒮
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}^{\mathcal{S}^2}
                classifies the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+model+homomorphisms"}
                  theory of
                  = succeed "-model" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕋
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                (with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕋
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
                classified by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℱ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝕋
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^2
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝕋
                              %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi 𝕋
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℰ
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_{\mathbb{T}^2}(\mathcal{E})=Mod_\mathbb{T}(\mathcal{E})^2
            %li
              %p
                The
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Malitz-Gregory topos
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Malitz-Gregory+topos"} ?
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable
                but has not
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
                (cf. Marquès
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Marq24"} 2024
          %h2#remarks_on_duality Remarks on duality
          %p
            It is worthwhile to muse a bit about
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E}
          %p
            First of at all, it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+topos"} injective
            since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]
            is injective and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (_-)^\mathcal{E}
            preserves inclusions.
          %p This and the various universal properties of the toposes involved imply that an exponentiable topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\cong Hom(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}])\cong Hom(\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{E},\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}])\cong Hom(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E})
          %p
            is (up to equivalence) the
            = succeed "." do
              %em category of points of an injective topos
          %p
            Now consider an arbitrary topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            classifying a geometric theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
          %p
            Then from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory#FunctorialDefinition"} functorial perspective on logic
            the 2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi GrTop
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^*:GrTop^{op}\to CAT
            assigning to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            the category of models
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕋
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^*(\mathcal{F}):=\mathcal{F}\times\mathcal{E}=\mathcal{F}\times\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{T}]
            is called the
            %strong dual theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
          %p
            It need not be geometric i.e. have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            but when it is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            being called
            %em dualizable
            in that case, the following
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^*(\mathcal{F})=\mathcal{F}\times\mathcal{E}\cong Hom(\mathcal{F}\times\mathcal{E},\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}])\cong Hom(\mathcal{F},\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E})
          %p
            shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕆
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E}
            has precisely the properties required for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕋
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{T}^*]
          %p
            In other words,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^*
            is geometric (and classified by
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi 𝕆
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^\mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝕋
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}=\mathcal{S}[\mathbb{T}]
            is exponentiable!
          %p
            Compare also the remarks of Anel (
            %a{:href => "#A15"}> 2015
            ) on the
            = succeed "-case." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topos"} initial topos
                that classifies the
                %em inconsistent theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝕋
                        %mn 1
                        %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^\emptyset_1
                over the empty signature. Then from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi 𝕆
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}[\mathbb{O}]^0=\mathcal{S}
                follows that the
                %em dual
                of the inconsistent theory is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝕋
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi ∅
                          %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝕋
                        %mi ∅
                        %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}_1^{\emptyset\ast}=\mathbb{T}_{\emptyset}^{\emptyset}
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝕋
                        %mi ∅
                        %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}_{\emptyset}^{\emptyset}
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+theory"} empty theory
                (over the empty signature).
            %li
              %p
