          %h3#the_theory_of_sheaves_on_a_coherent_site The theory of sheaves on a coherent site
          %p
            Recall, that given a small site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},J)
            there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_J
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+flat+functors"} theory of J-continuous flat functors
            that (albeit uneconomically) axiomaticizes the theory classified by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C},J)
            using the objects and morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            for its signature. When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(\mathcal{C},J)
            is exponentiable this theory is dualizable, and, in the case the site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},J_c)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+site"} coherent
            i. e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
